    "title": "Anatomy Of A Riot - July 1967 - Past Daily Reference Room - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By gordonskene ,\n7 hours ago – NBC Radio: Second Sunday – Newark: Anatomy Of A Riot – July 1967 – Gordon Skene Sound Collection. No end to turmoil sweeping over American cities in the decade of the 1960s. The rise of poverty and unemployment, and the rapid decay of Urban areas were all ingredients of a potentially chaotic situation. Coupled with that phenomenon known as “white flight” where the mass exodus of whites from urban areas (a phenomenon which began after the war with the advent of suburbia) left many inner cities in a state of desolation and where many factories relocated to other parts of the country, turning once thriving urban centers into wastelands. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
